extends RefCounted
## All essential dialogue also appears as text; no recorded speech is required.

const INTRO := """11:47 PM. Nirva Halt has been closed for twelve years.
Aarav Sen, seventeen, has searched for his older brother ever since.

Rohan's first message sounds like him: 'Aarav, if you're hearing this,
don't let them announce the train.'

The second contains only three words: 'Platform Three. Midnight.'"""

const LOGBOOK := """19 JULY 2014 — Train 03 vanished beyond Nirva Halt.
The manifest says every passenger was still aboard.

A handwritten relay procedure survives in the margin:
First give them LAMP light. Then ring the BELL.
Only then wake the LINE.

The last name on the passenger list has been rubbed away."""

const TIMETABLE := """NIRVA HALT — FINAL DEPARTURES
Train 03: ARRIVAL 11:59 PM / DEPARTURE 12:00 AM

Someone has crossed out ARRIVAL and written:
'If the station says it arrived, the doors will open.'

On the reverse: 'Rohan, do not answer the loudspeaker.'"""

const FEED := """PLATFORM THREE / SECURITY ARCHIVE
The camera clock reads 11:47 PM. Its date is 19 July 2014.

A young man stands by the signal post with a station logbook.
When the frame skips, he is closer to the camera.

The passenger database is offline. Emergency power may restore it."""

const TRANSCRIPT := """OPERATOR'S TRANSCRIPT — LAST SHIFT
11:58: A male voice on Platform Three requests the passenger list.
11:59: Automatic announcement begins before any train is seen.

Operator's note: 'It called every name, even a child who never boarded.
I pulled the speaker line. For a moment, the train vanished.'

The archive ends with Rohan asking who wrote the list."""

const MEMO := """EMERGENCY RELAY / REWIRED AFTER THE INCIDENT
3 — LAMP     1 — BELL     2 — LINE

The logbook describes the order. Pulling the wrong relay trips
all three breakers; begin again from darkness.

Speaker cut-off is beside the service phone on Platform Three."""

const PASSENGERS := """TRAIN 03 — BOARDING RECORD / 19 JULY 2014
Seat 17: ROHAN SEN — marked ABOARD
Seat 18: AARAV SEN — age 05 — marked EXPECTED

Aarav never boarded that train. He was five in 2014.
The word EXPECTED is fresh, as though it has just been typed.

The security feed now shows Rohan beside the platform phone."""

const CALL := """ROHAN / INCOMING CALL
'Aarav, listen carefully. It is using my voice because you came.
I stayed to stop the announcement. I couldn't reach the switch.

The speaker cut-off is near this phone. Pull it before the train
opens its doors. Whatever the list says, do not step inside.'

The line clicks. Through the rain, two lights approach."""

const ENDING := """Aarav cuts the speaker before it can finish his name.
The platform lights fail. Train 03 retreats without opening a door.

For one clear second Rohan's real voice returns:
'You did it. Keep those notes. Don't come back for me tonight.'

The entrance unlocks. Aarav leaves Nirva Halt with his notes.
Rohan is still missing, but the station did not claim another passenger.

THE END  /  THE LAST SIGNAL"""
